From: XR1710G Maintainer <maintainer@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: bridge: map VLAN-aware bridge PVID to VLAN device

When bridge-nf-call-iptables or bridge-nf-call-ip6tables is enabled,
br_netfilter passes bridged packets through the inet hooks.  For a
VLAN-aware bridge, an untagged access port has no skb VLAN tag: its VLAN
identity is the port PVID.  brnf_get_logical_dev() currently returns the
bridge master for such packets even when bridge-nf-pass-vlan-input-dev is
enabled.  Consequently firewall4 rules matching br-lan.<vid> do not match
and the default forward policy drops WiFi access-port traffic.

When VLAN input-device passing is requested and VLAN filtering is active,
look up the ingress port PVID for untagged packets and resolve the matching
VLAN upper device of the bridge.  Tagged ingress keeps the existing path.
This preserves the per-VLAN netfilter ingress context while allowing
nft_flow_offload to create a bridge/PPE flow.

Signed-off-by: XR1710G Maintainer <maintainer@example.com>
---
 net/bridge/br_netfilter_hooks.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/net/bridge/br_netfilter_hooks.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_netfilter_hooks.c
@@ -434,12 +434,26 @@ static struct net_device *brnf_get_logical_dev
 	struct net_device *vlan, *br;
 	struct brnf_net *brnet = net_generic(net, brnf_net_id);
+	struct net_bridge_port *port;
+	u16 vid;
 
	br = bridge_parent(dev);
 
-	if (brnet->pass_vlan_indev == 0 || !skb_vlan_tag_present(skb))
+	if (brnet->pass_vlan_indev == 0)
 		return br;
 
-	vlan = __vlan_find_dev_deep_rcu(br, skb->vlan_proto,
-				    skb_vlan_tag_get(skb) & VLAN_VID_MASK);
+	if (skb_vlan_tag_present(skb)) {
+		vid = skb_vlan_tag_get(skb) & VLAN_VID_MASK;
+	} else {
+		/* An access port carries its VLAN identity in the PVID, not skb. */
+		port = br_port_get_rcu(dev);
+		if (!port || !br_opt_get(port->br, BROPT_VLAN_ENABLED) ||
+		    br_vlan_get_pvid_rcu(dev, &vid) || !vid)
+			return br;
+	}
+
+	if (skb_vlan_tag_present(skb))
+		vlan = __vlan_find_dev_deep_rcu(br, skb->vlan_proto, vid);
+	else
+		vlan = __vlan_find_dev_deep_rcu(br, port->br->vlan_proto, vid);
 
 	return vlan ? vlan : br;
